      "notes": "Gentle rise-and-fall, singable range and shape -- meant to read as a lead vocal line, not a horn riff or a jazz-development exercise. Between the fanfare's punch and the ballad's long arc in length -- 8 notes, 1 bar, but legato rather than syncopated."
    },
    "notes": "Chill 70s soft-rock ballad -- the 'If You Leave Me Now' side of this band's sound, not the horn-stab 'Wall of Brass' side. Functional ionian harmony (not modal), warm maj9/m9 chords throughout, a borrowed minor iv (ivm7, from the parallel minor -- classic soft-rock/soul-ballad bittersweet lift right before resolving home) in the chorus, and one secondary dominant (V7(9)/vi) for a gentle lift into the relative minor. bass_style='melodic' for a singing, moving bassline rather than the previous pieces' pedal drone or driving pulse. voicing='open' for lush pad spacing. No drums in the verse (intimate, rubato-adjacent feel); a soft halftime pattern only enters for the chorus.",
